        "id": "disc_1",
        "title": "Architecting Server Components with GraphQL Yoga in Next.js App Router",
        "slug": "architecting-server-components-with-graphql-yoga-in-nextjs-app-router",
        "content": "When building high-performance modern web apps, balancing Next.js Server Components with a flexible GraphQL layer can dramatically streamline state management and payload size.\n\n```typescript\n// GraphQL Yoga Route in Next.js App Router\nexport async function POST(req: Request) {\n  return yoga.handleRequest(req, {});\n}\n```\n\nWhat are your experiences handling cache invalidation between RSC and client GraphQL queries?",
        "pinned": true,
        "solved": true,
        "score": 24,
        "upvotesCount": 25,
        "downvotesCount": 1,
        "commentsCount": 2,
        "viewsCount": 342,
